{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310657,"nonce":"3pQ76d9zxHabz74zbnM4l71YgrY=","title":"Sharing cached stdlib MIR for only the non-generic modules ALSO breaks — hypothesis falsified 2026-08-17; the fix is to cache declarations, ...","message":"**ATTEMPTED, MEASURED, REVERTED (2026-08-17, at `9875ac20`). Do not retry the\nper-module split.**\n\n`e4ec2b11` had reverted cross-program stdlib cache sharing because\n`Channel\u003cT\u003e`/`Tls\u003cT\u003e` are lowered against the instantiations their program\nsupplies. The obvious refinement: share only modules that declare NO generic,\nkeep the program in the key for the rest. Of haxe-std's 240 modules only 57\ndeclare a generic; in the 42-module `Sys.println` closure the split is 13\ngeneric / 29 plain.\n\n**IT WORKED, AND IT IS STILL UNSOUND.**\n\nMeasured with the split in (`is_program_independent_stdlib` =\n`is_stdlib_source \u0026\u0026 !declares_generic`, skipping the `user_program_hash()`\nfold):\n- second, different program: `cache_hit=36 miss=6`, tc.imports 250ms → **29ms**,\n  compile 249ms → **42ms**\n- the documented Map/StringTools/Sys silent-miscompile repro prints `q`\n  correctly in BOTH orders\n- `run_haxe_tests.sh` **184/184**, including all three channel canaries that\n  forced `e4ec2b11` (`Channel\u003cT\u003e` is generic, so it is never shared)\n\n**BUT:** `test_sys_thread` fails 2 tests and `test_rayzor_stdlib_e2e` dies with\n`fatal runtime error: stack overflow` — COLD AND WARM. Both pass with the\nchange reverted; confirmed by stashing it and rebuilding. That stack overflow\nis the same \"unbounded recursion in type resolution\" `e4ec2b11` names.\n\n**THE HYPOTHESIS IS DEAD: \"declares no generic ⇒ its lowering is\nprogram-independent\" is FALSE.** A module that declares nothing generic still\nUSES generics, and the instantiated/monomorphised state it is lowered against\ncomes from the program. Do not look for a cleverer syntactic rule — the\nproperty is not a property of the module's own text.\n\n**THE DIRECTION INSTEAD — cache DECLARATIONS, not lowered MIR.** zyntax\n(`crates/typed_ast/src/import_resolver.rs`) caches `ExportedSymbol` /\n`ResolvedImport` / `Type` — the signature level — which is program-independent\nby construction. rayzor's `.blade` cache stores lowered MIR, which is exactly\nthe part that carries program-relative state. rayzor already has the\ndeclaration-level artifact (`.bsym`), but per\n[[perf_bsym_manifest_is_net_negative_on_cold_start]] it ADDS registration and\nREMOVES nothing — the 12 defaults are still parsed. Making the manifest serve\ndeclarations so the modules are never parsed/typechecked is the sound version\nof this win, and it targets the same 255ms.\n\n**MEASUREMENT NOTE:** cold start IS the `rm -rf .rayzor` case — do not dismiss\nit as an artifact. Warm is 0.05s and never reaches the profiler. The number to\nmove is the cold one.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_nongeneric_stdlib_modules_still_program_dependent` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}